   "updated": 1,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "type": "text",
   "id": "ivnt389",
   "x": 1512.75,
   "y": 3846.875,
   "width": 874.5000000000001,
   "height": 56.25,
   "text": "Interview answer: 'Replicas are stateless: every graph state lives in Postgres under its thread_id, so any\nreplica can resume a paused review. Scale by adding replicas behind a gateway, pool the DB connections,\nand let the gateway handle auth and rate limits. The LLM provider's rate limit is the real ceiling.'",
   "originalText": "Interview answer: 'Replicas are stateless: every graph state lives in Postgres under its thread_id, so any\nreplica can resume a paused review. Scale by adding replicas behind a gateway, pool the DB connections,\nand let the gateway handle auth and rate limits. The LLM provider's rate limit is the real ceiling.'",
   "fontSize": 15,
   "fontFamily": 1,
   "lineHeight": 1.25,
   "textAlign": "center",
   "verticalAlign": "middle",
   "containerId": "ivr226",
   "autoResize": true
  }
